eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philwo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/milestones/5","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/milestone/5","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/milestones/5/labels","id":1717213,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMTcxNzIxMw==","number":5,"title":"0.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"damienmg","id":3721087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjEwODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3721087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg","html_url":"https://github.com/damienmg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":158,"state":"closed","created_at":"2016-04-19T15:07:50Z","updated_at":"2020-05-12T11:10:23Z","due_on":"2017-06-30T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2017-11-29T19:06:44Z"},"comments":20,"created_at":"2016-10-20T21:46:50Z","updated_at":"2023-11-27T11:20:20Z","closed_at":"2017-05-02T19:43:47Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"When trying to build anything with the new sandbox and Debian Jessie's amd64 default 3.16.0-4 kernel, it fails with `src/main/tools/linux-sandbox-pid1.cc:393: \"mount\": Operation not permitted`. @philsc and I have previously looked for ways to make /proc show the right PIDs in a PID namespace on that kernel without root permission and not come up with anything.\n\nI don't have any good answers in the way of solutions. asan definitely does not do well with a broken /proc (that's what @philsc and I were working on previously, although we ran into other, more fundamental issues and gave up), and from what I've seen of java it won't either. However, having a PID namespace is really nice for preventing runaway processes (I periodically have to use pgrep and manually kill runaway test process with the old sandbox).\n\nThese commands show the same issue with that kernel:\n\n``` console\nbrian[907] dev-builder ~:\n$ unshare --mount --map-root-user --pid --fork\nroot[857] dev-builder ~:\n# mount -t proc proc /proc\nmount: permission denied\nroot[857] dev-builder ~:\n```\n\nThose same commands succeed with 4.3.0-0 kernel from jessie-backports, so I'm pretty sure Bazel's sandbox will too (haven't checked though):\n\n``` console\nbrian[17107] brian-debian ~:\n$ unshare --mount --map-root-user --pid --fork\nroot[501] brian-debian ~:\n# mount -t proc proc /proc\nroot[501] brian-debian ~:\n```\n\n/cc @philwo \n","closed_by":{"login":"brian-peloton","id":7906026,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDYwMjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7906026?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-peloton","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-peloton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-peloton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-peloton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-peloton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-peloton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/us